      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6e29aea567a1e97de89ad5175847af39d0ba634b3f1edcdf485502bc86207fbd",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Functional-equation phases act as a global filter on dual configurations in conjectural family moments. In the prime-level one-level-density calculation, splitting by root-number sign inserts a root-number-coupled Petersson term whose factored Kloosterman and principal-character contribution survives with opposite signs, whereas it cancels in the mixed family; this parity channel is distinct from leading local equidistribution and persistent central rank.",
