    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c30afc5ce8d09fa9934d12de92350fa3ffc3d69fea6e8ea6c84e29168831a4a9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The general L-function template separates Euler-factor multiplicativity from completed reflection symmetry. For modular eigenforms those features arise through compatible but distinct structures: simultaneous Hecke eigenvectors make Fourier coefficients multiplicative and yield local factors, while modular transformation together with completion yields the functional equation.",
