    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_dd9a1133485b720d03a7b1de2dc28f64e73e2c24af7067af86d4682286fae2b0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Zeta completion clears the pole, adds the gamma factor, and recenters reflection so that RH becomes real-rootedness of an even entire function. For a nonreal Dirichlet character, pairing the dual character factors, with the appropriate completion understood, internalizes their conjugate functional equation in one self-symmetric object whose zero divisor is the union of the two factors' divisors.",
