      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f5c5d0719b2a89b6b2684912c4e6069a2b35bdb3d138ada7ba1943b17d40d316",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Zero statistics and explicit formulas specify constraints that a spectral model should reproduce, but reproduction is only an encoding test. A useful Hilbert–Polya or geometric construction must be independent of the zero set and add a self-adjoint, positive, or index-type mechanism that forces location rather than merely restating the spectrum.",
